<section id="palettes-demo" class="demo" data-flux="flux-first-visible">
	<h2>Image and video palettes</h2><p>Flux samples the image or current video frame at a small size. CSS uses the dominant, accent, dark, light and average colours. Video sampling pauses off-screen.</p>
	<div class="demo-grid">
		<figure class="palette-preview" data-flux="flux-palette"><img src="?asset=palette.svg" width="640" height="360" alt="Layered hills beneath a golden sun" /><figcaption>Image palette</figcaption><div class="swatches" aria-label="Accent, dark, light and average colours"><span class="accent"></span><span class="dark"></span><span class="light"></span><span class="average"></span></div><div class="temperature" aria-label="Colour temperature"><span></span></div></figure>
		<figure class="palette-preview" data-flux="flux-palette"><video src="?asset=palette.webm" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" width="320" height="180" aria-label="A silent colour study"></video><figcaption>Play the video to update its palette</figcaption><div class="swatches" aria-label="Accent, dark, light and average colours"><span class="accent"></span><span class="dark"></span><span class="light"></span><span class="average"></span></div><div class="temperature" aria-label="Colour temperature"><span></span></div></figure>
	</div>
	<p>These files are served by this site. Media hosted elsewhere needs permission through CORS for the browser to read its pixels.</p>
</section>
